From 21b6765da487cf4f0d089a0f5074b8ea4166a251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElixirOffice contributors <noreply@elixiroffice.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:49:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DOCX: picture bullets are kept through the binary format

A list level whose bullet is a picture (w:lvlPicBulletId, pointing at a
w:numPicBullet) had no place in the editor's binary format, so the
picture was dropped on the way in and the .docx came back with a text
bullet. The numbering table now carries the pictures, each with its id,
its file in the media folder and its size, and the level its picture's
id; the picture is written back as a relationship of numbering.xml, and
numPicBullet goes first in it, as CT_Numbering wants.

From ElixirOffice's core, commit 854f6e1 (their 0.7.2), the part of it
that carries picture bullets; sdkjs 0011 reads and draws them.
